 "notes": [
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 45,
   "sec": 3,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Canals in the north:** Canal irrigation is strongest in the northern plains because the Himalayan rivers are perennial (snow-fed) and can feed canals all year; peninsular areas rely more on tanks."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 46,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Drip irrigation:** sends water straight to the root zone of plants; soluble fertiliser can be given through the same lines (fertigation)."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 48,
   "sec": 5,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Chemical pesticides:** act quickly with high efficacy; drawbacks are residues in food, harm to friendly insects and pest resistance, so IPM uses them only when needed."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 48,
   "sec": 9,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Meghdoot app (2019):** mobile app that gives farmers weather-based agro-meteorological advisories in local languages."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 48,
   "sec": 7,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **PMKSY type:** an umbrella Centrally Sponsored Scheme launched in 2015-16 (1 July 2015), with AIBP, Har Khet Ko Pani, Per Drop More Crop and Watershed components."
  }
 ],
